(1962109, 268258, 3569, '<td valign="top">I couldn''t resist.  My 11 year old daughter dancing and singing for our Children''s Christmas Church Service.  Knew it wasn''t the best, but I''m a proud Papa.  And it Christmas Season indeed.<br/> <br/>Taken from 100+ ft. 400mm at ISO 1600 at 1/100 at F4.  So I knew it was iffy.<br/> <br/>Thanks for the comments and one 10<br/><br/><i>Message edited by author 2005-12-19 09:24:48.</i></td>', 'I couldn''t resist.  My 11 year old daughter dancing and singing for our Children''s Christmas Church Service.  Knew it wasn''t the best, but I''m a proud Papa.  And it Christmas Season indeed. Taken from 100+ ft. 400mm at ISO 1600 at 1/100 at F4.  So I knew it was iffy. Thanks for the comments and one 10', '2005-12-19 08:01:46.000000', '2005-12-19 09:24:48.000000', 0),
(1962208, 268179, 28710, '<td valign="top">Too funny.<br/> <br/>Personally, I think this could be improved by using a minitripod and putting the 20d a little farther forward to make it more prominent in the picture. The charger could stand to be hidden somewhere else. Charging batteries doesn''t seem to be the primary goal of Canon-eers, let alone a desirable activity to all those Nikon-eers who are secretly desiring Canon Goodness.<br/> <br/>Additionally, the lights could stand to be strung up in a slightly less haphazard way.<br/> <br/>Of course what most Nikon-eers really want is the D200, so they can keep all their existing glass...</td>', 'Too funny. Personally, I think this could be improved by using a minitripod and putting the 20d a little farther forward to make it more prominent in the picture. The charger could stand to be hidden somewhere else. Charging batteries doesn''t seem to be the primary goal of Canon-eers, let alone a desirable activity to all those Nikon-eers who are secretly desiring Canon Goodness. Additionally, the lights could stand to be strung up in a slightly less haphazard way. Of course what most Nikon-eers really want is the D200, so they can keep all their existing glass...', '2005-12-19 09:26:02.000000', NULL, 0);
